        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T16:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would using the build-time flag here mean we don\u0027t need to deal with unsupported errors?\n\nThat is... can we count on all devices that expose the HAL to also fully support the RKP VM? If so, that\u0027s the ideal solution I think.",
      "parentUuid": "c65462a2_8ec6d4dd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "9617241914a27d029a4b6e4a46e84a78153c3e79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f25de80_5b94afb8",
        "filename": "apex/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T16:15:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m afraid not.\n\nThe flag is mostly to cover us on pre-V releases - none of these changes should be visible there, regardless of AVF support.\n\nBut we need to return unsupported on devices that support AVF but only for non-protected VMs. Currently we can only determine that at runtime.",
      "parentUuid": "65055006_8a34e389",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "9617241914a27d029a4b6e4a46e84a78153c3e79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
